    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39708" root="نسب" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا الشِّعْرُ أَنْسَبُ</span></b>  <i>This poetry is more,</i> or <i>most.
elegant in what is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَسِيب</span>. see 2: (K:)
as though they had said <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَسِيبٌ نَاسِبٌ</span>, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِعْرٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاعِرٌ</span>, to give intensiveness to the signification,
and thence formed the word <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْسَبُ</span>. (TA.)

